Camera detection delivery development qualification. No images or credentials.

The unchanged MIT PICO model, pinned ESP-DL numerical implementation and frozen
accuracy samples are documented in ../2026-10-22-pico and their earlier sources.
These reports measure metadata delivery and concurrent physical video, not a
new dataset or security-reliability result.

endurance.json records a 600-second real-camera WHEP decode with simultaneous
schema-validated authenticated SSE. Initial/final and ten-second serial samples
are retained. Heap numbers are used bytes and include bounded frame/decoder
allocations; a range is not a leak estimate. Firmware hashes identify the actual
flashed image. Gateway file hashes identify rebuilt host executable files only,
as explicitly scoped in that report. No private host addresses, capture images,
source-session identifiers or runtime enrollment are retained.

video-off.json removes only device_ip, stream_port and image_path from the
final image's direct-MJPEG detection-disabled control. That control and the
WHEP endurance use different host decoding paths and both exclude startup.
stack-control.json records the rejected 16 KiB owner-stack margin. Firmware
source hashes and the final 32 KiB task budget are independently checked.

native-ios.json uses the same DetectionSession and URLSession transport as the
app, executing on an owned disposable iOS Simulator with existing fixture CA
trust installed only in that Simulator. The normal app was also built against
Simulator and iPhone SDKs. UI navigation validates layout and unavailable status
with the explicitly labeled design fixture, not with a fabricated live image.
No physical-iPhone detection acceptance, frame-aligned boxes, push notifications,
night/IR qualification or multi-day endurance is claimed.
